Personal documents such as diaries, identification cards, utility bills, receipts and bank statements were spread across the dining room table and the sofa on the second floor. In the bathtub, police found some of Mikio's work documents, receipts, Yasuko's cram school paperwork, sanitary items, towels, ice cream wrappers and the random contents of a drawer that had been emptied. Stolen from the home was a tuition fee paid by one of Yasuko's students, which amounted to approximately 200,000 yen, the equivalent of around 3,000 Australian dollars at the time.
日记、身份证件、公用事业账单、收据和银行对账单等个人文件散落在二楼的餐桌和沙发上。在浴缸里，警察发现了一些干男的工作文件、收据、泰子的补习班文件、卫生用品、毛巾、冰淇淋包装纸和一个被清空抽屉里的杂物。从家中被盗的是泰子的一名学生支付的学费，金额约为20万日元，相当于当时大约3000澳元。

