bum bag in Australia or fanny pack in the United States. It was 21 cm wide, 23.5 cm high and 9.5 cm deep, which equated to the approximate size of a B5 notebook. The belt secured to the bag was 83 cm long but had been adjusted to fit a waist measuring between 70 and 75 cm. The bag was old and worn and also came with a shoulder strap so it could be used as a pouchel. It was manufactured in Osaka between 1995 and 1999 with 2,850 sold at discount stores
