In 2003, family, friends and supporters of the Slain family hosted a photography exhibition featuring images of the Mayor's Hours that were returned from police earlier that year. Among the collection was a photo of Nina cuddling her newborn baby brother, Rayi, and another of the family gathered happily around a birthday cake to celebrate Rayi's second birthday. One of the exhibition's organisers said, We want people not to just think about how heinous the crime was, but also how happy the family was in life. Given that the killer's sneakers were sold exclusively in South Korea and the soil particles from his jacket pocket were also traced back to the same country, Japanese investigators
