titled If You Can Understand The Meaning Of This Sadness, The Setagaya Case, The Story of Loss and Rebirth. That same month, Japan's National Police Agency announced that a reward of 3 million yen, the equivalent of 30,000 Australian dollars at the time, was available for information regarding the Miyazawa family case. In the following year, it was reported that Japanese police had asked authorities in China, the United States, and some Western countries to provide fingerprint records to compare against their suspect. But it is unclear what progress, if any, was made. At the time the murders were committed, Japan had a 15-year statute of limitations on murder charges,
书名为《如果你能理解这种悲伤的含义：世田谷案件，失去与重生的故事》。同月，日本警察厅宣布，提供有关宫泽家族案件线索的悬赏金为300万日元，相当于当时的3万澳元。第二年，据报道日本警察已要求中国、美国和一些西方国家的当局提供指纹记录，以便与他们的嫌疑人进行比对。但目前还不清楚取得了什么进展（如果有的话）。在谋杀案发生时，日本对谋杀罪有15年的诉讼时效，

